Currently, in Apache Spark's {{JdbcUtils}} (across all versions, including Spark 4), there is no support for complex types like {{{}StructType{}}}, {{{}MapType{}}}, except for {{{}ArrayType{}}}. This limitation is evident in the private methods [makeGetter|https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/6246b18635f073e872e32dd05a699007446aee94/sql/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/execution/datasources/jdbc/JdbcUtils.scala#L400] and [makeSetter|https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/6246b18635f073e872e32dd05a699007446aee94/sql/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/execution/datasources/jdbc/JdbcUtils.scala#L620].

As Spark provides the ability to implement custom dialects, users cannot implement custom handling for these complex types because the methods are private and they encounter the following error:

 

{{org.apache.spark.SparkSQLException: Unsupported type <complex_type>.}}

The suggestion is to change the way these methods are called. Specifically, the getter/setter methods should be able to be provided by the `JdbcDialect`, rather than only being hardcoded in `JdbcUtils`.

I suppose it can be done in one of two ways:

1. Modify the makeGetter and makeSetter methods to delegate to the dialect
    
   {code}
    
    class JdbcUtils {
      def makeGetter(args): Option[Getter] = {
        dialect.makeGetter(args).orElse {
          ...
        }
      }
    
      def makeSetter(args): Option[Setter] = {
        dialect.makeSetter(args).orElse {
          ...
        }
      }
    }
   {code}
    
2. Move the makeGetter/makeSetter methods out of JdbcUtils into JdbcDialect, allowing custom dialects to override them. 
    
    {code}
    
    abstract class JdbcDialect {
      def makeGetter(args): Option[Getter]
      def makeSetter(args): Option[Setter]
    }
    
    object JdbcUtils {
      def getGetter(args): Option[Getter] = {
        // logic to fetch getter from JdbcDialect
      }
    
      def getSetter(args): Option[Setter] = {
        // logic to fetch setter from JdbcDialect
      }
    }
   {code}

Currently, in Apache Spark's {{JdbcUtils}} (across all versions, including Spark 4), there is no support for {{{}StructType{}}}, {{MapType.}}

The current implementation in {{JdbcUtils}} supports [{{ArrayType}}|https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/6246b18635f073e872e32dd05a699007446aee94/sql/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/execution/datasources/jdbc/JdbcUtils.scala#L687]

To extend the functionality and enable users to read and write {{StructType}} and {{MapType}} from their databases analog, it is proposed to add similar handling for these complex types in the {{makeGetter}} and {{makeSetter}} methods.

For {{MapType}} it might look like:

{code:java}
case MapType(keyType, valueType, valueContainsNull) =>
  (rs: ResultSet, row: InternalRow, pos: Int) =>
    val mapData = rs.getObject(pos + 1).asInstanceOf[Map[Any, Any]]
    if (mapData == null) {
      row.setNullAt(pos)
    } else {
      val keys = mapData.keys.map(getCatalystType(keyType).getJavaValue).toArray
      val values = mapData.values.map(getCatalystType(valueType).getJavaValue).toArray
      row.update(pos, new ArrayBasedMapData(new GenericArrayData(keys), new GenericArrayData(values)))
    } {code}

