Currently {{VectorizedRleValuesReader}} reads short in the following way:
{code:java}
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
  c.putShort(rowId + i, (short)data.readInteger());
}
{code}

For PLAIN encoding {{readInteger}} is done via:
{code:java}
public final int readInteger() {
  return getBuffer(4).getInt();
}
{code}
which means it needs to repeatedly call {{slice}} buffer which is more expensive than calling it once in a big chunk and then reading the ints out.

