This is a corner case that https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SPARK-44940 missed.

For a query like the following:

{{SELECT}}
{{  GET_JSON_OBJECT(json_col, '$.a.b'),}}
{{  GET_JSON_OBJECT(json_col, '$.a.c')}}
{{FROM t}}

SparkSQL would generate a plan that parse the json_col twice.

Ideally, SparkSQL should only parse the `json_col` once.  The optimizer should find out the common JSON parsing, and modify the plan to parse the JSON once, get the result out, and flatten it back.

An alternative way to support this is the ":" notation (JSON Path) as in other systems where the query optimizer will automatically share a single JSON parsing.

