Hi

In a recent discussion I discovered there was a misunderstanding in ML doc, taking its origin in chosen examples:  I think the clarity of documentation could be improved by only changing the values of vector in documentation.

Examples of misleading vector
{quote}{{dv = Vectors.dense(1.0, 0.0, 3.0);}}
{{{}sv = Vectors.sparse(3, new int[] {0, 2}, new double[] {1.0, 3.0});{}}}{{{}{}}}{{{}{}}}
{quote}
As you can see, the vector chosen in example has ordinal position of element as value, and has 3 elements wich is also value of 3rd element, which is also the size of the vector.  I understood this has been leading to confusion in the reader comprehesion (a newbie, not native english speaker) 

The example would gain in  understanding with example values  like this
{quote}{{{}dv = Vectors.dense(7.0, 0.0, 5.0);
{}}}{{{}sv = Vectors.sparse(3, new int[] {0, 2}, new double[] {7.0, 5.0});{}}}{{{}{}}}
{quote}
 

This ticket is a proposal to update docs using vector (1.0, 0.0, 3.0) into vector (7.0, 0.0, 5.0)

